#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Compression arc session C (notes/adr/0145-rulings-standing-register.md).

Run ONCE, on 2026-08-17, to make `.agents/rulings.md` what its own header
has claimed since ADR-0047 and has not been since roughly ADR-0057: a
register of STANDING RULES ONLY, not a history.

    - **R-<slug>** -- <rule> -- ADR-NNNN [SUPERSEDED-BY R-<slug> (ADR-NNNN)]

gated by `ehrt.docs-tooling.rulings-lint-test`.

Two things happen, and only these two:

  1. Every `## From ...` block leaves the file VERBATIM, appended to the
     ADR that owns it (an arc block goes to that arc's own close ADR)
     under a dated heading. Nothing is summarised, nothing is deleted.
     The file's own current header goes the same way, to ADR-0145.
  2. The STANDING and SUPERSEDED rulings the census classified become
     rows, authored from the bullets they replace, each citing the ADR
     that ruled it. An ARC-LOCAL bullet becomes no row: its text now
     lives in its own ADR, which is where an execution decision belongs.

The judgement -- which of 181 bullets is a standing rule, which is an
executed-once decision, which was superseded and by what -- is authored,
in BULLETS below, each entry carrying the sentence that decides it. What
is mechanical, and what this script does, is the move and the read-back.

Usage:
    bin/rulings-migrate-0145 --markdown   # the census, as ADR tables
    bin/rulings-migrate-0145 --dry-run    # what would be written
    bin/rulings-migrate-0145              # do it
    bin/rulings-migrate-0145 --verify     # read every block back out

`--verify` re-reads `.agents/rulings.md` as it was at the pinned base
commit and asserts each moved block is present as an exact contiguous
block at its destination NOW. That, not `git diff --numstat`, is the
instrument: ADR-0144 found a diffstat cannot express a move of this
shape as an identity, because git renders moved lines that duplicate
adjacent content as context rather than insertions.
"""

import os
